## ANSI test artifacts (generated at project root)
*.txt
# ...except the per-case method maps, which are the comparator's input, not output.
!bench/il-parity/*/methods.txt
# ...except the library-status target list: it is generated, but from dist
# metadata rather than from a run, so it is checked in and reviewed as the input
# to the next stage (bench/library-status/README.md).
!bench/library-status/targets.txt
# ...and the hand-picked list, which is the opposite: written by hand and read
# by rank.lisp, so losing it would lose the only record of why those targets
# are on the list at all.
!bench/library-status/hand-picked.txt
*.fasl
# Ahead-of-time siblings (<name>.fasl.r2r-<rid>, dotcl.core.r2r-<rid>). The
# marker sits after the whole filename so that *.fasl globs do not match one,
# which also means this rule has to name them itself.
*.r2r-*
*.ufsl
*.tmp
test/regression/.tmp-*/
*.sil
# ...except the legacy .sil fixtures: they are checked in precisely because they
# are output, emitted by a released dotcl and never regenerated.
!test/regression/legacy-sil/*.sil
/*.lsp
compile-file-*
COMPILE-FILE-*
load-test-file*
modules[0-9]*
sandbox/

# Non-source artifacts under docs/ (talk media, editor backups)
docs/**/*.mp4
docs/**/*~
out/
# Disposable build artifacts: the pinned seed install, the selfhost stages, and
# the marker that keeps all of it out of a scanning source registry.
/build/
runtime/contrib/
contrib/asdf/
contrib/quicklisp/

